      "statement": "The packet-write transaction wrapper defines a read-decide-mutate boundary in PostgreSQL: it reads canonical state, applies only a guarded mutation for an advancing revision or a qualified insert, writes a projection outbox event only when a mutation occurs, and writes a receipt for every decision while leaving external projection work to a later consumer; the wrapper is explicitly scaffolding rather than proof that every live writer routes through it.",
